Ladybird applies an element’s clip-path, clip and masks to its filtered
output. Gecko’s nsIFrame::BuildDisplayListForStackingContext() wraps
the contents in nsDisplayFilters first, and then wraps that in
nsDisplayMasksAndClipPaths. Blink’s FragmentPaintPropertyTreeBuilder
builds the clip-path clip, the effect node holding the mask, and the CSS
clip all outside the filter node: It calls UpdateClipPathClip(),
UpdateEffect() and UpdateCssClip() before UpdateFilter().
